STATUS
PASS / POLICY-FROZEN

ACCESS MODES
MODE A CORE OWNED: SUPPORTED / PASS ON WINDOWS
External Runtime -> External Agent Protocol -> AgentControl -> Core -> Repository

MODE B EMBEDDED: SUPPORTED INTERNAL / EMBEDDED
Rust library embedding, tests, cold reopen, offline tooling, migration, and
maintenance may use Repository directly while no Core owner is active.

MODE C DIRECT MULTI-PROCESS EXTERNAL: NOT_SUPPORTED
Independent external Runtime processes do not directly open Repository.

PRODUCTION PATH AUDIT
pong-agent-protocol uses Repository::open_as_core_owner. No production-facing
External Runtime path directly opens Repository or MetadataStore. The M4-010
filesystem broker is a test harness and does not change JSONL transport.

NEGATIVE SAFETY TEST
repository_access_policy::unsupported_direct_multi_process_access_fails_closed
PASS. Two real direct-access probe processes were rejected with CONFLICT while
one Core owner held the Repository. After owner shutdown, cold reopen passed,
the marker was unchanged, and no probe Operation existed.

The existing M4-008 direct-writer diagnostics remain active. The Workspace
publication diagnostic now records OPEN versus SNAPSHOT failure and validates
cold-reopen Workspace heads before asserting that an OS result is classified.
Its accepted error set was not widened and no test was ignored or serialized.

OS ERROR CLASSIFICATION
WouldBlock at owner lock: repository access CONFLICT.
Windows 32: ERROR_SHARING_VIOLATION, access conflict.
Windows 33: ERROR_LOCK_VIOLATION, access conflict.
Windows 2: context-dependent transient namespace race, not a global conflict.
Windows 5: ambiguous ACL denial or access/share race, NOT_PROVEN. It remains
PERMISSION_DENIED at protected repository boundaries.
Linux/macOS parity: NOT_PROVEN.

CODE 5 INVESTIGATION
The prior M4-010 full regression observed code 5 in a combined direct
Repository open/snapshot child path. Thirty focused reruns after phase
instrumentation did not reproduce code 5. They observed successful publication,
open-time code 33, and one open-time code 2. No global reclassification was
made because Pong also has native Windows ACL evidence for code 5.

